    "prompt": "You are ForecastBot's SINGLE forecasting agent.\n\nYou are responsible for understanding the user's forecasting request and\ngenerating the SQL needed to retrieve the corresponding time series.\n\nUSER REQUEST:\nTôi muốn dự báo lượng bán của sản phẩm FOODS_3_629 tại cửa hàng TX_3, bang TX trong 90 ngày tới.\n\nEXPECTED DATASET FOR THIS EVALUATION CASE:\nM5\n\nDATABASE SCHEMA KNOWLEDGE:\n\nDataset: M5\n\nYou are working with a PostgreSQL database for M5 retail sales forecasting.\n\n1. Table: m5_sales_train\n- id (TEXT): Unique series identifier\n- item_id (TEXT): Product identifier\n- dept_id (TEXT): Department identifier\n- cat_id (TEXT): Category identifier\n- store_id (TEXT): Store identifier\n- state_id (TEXT): State identifier\n- d (TEXT): Day key, not a real calendar date\n- sales (NUMERIC): Daily sales quantity\n\n2. Table: m5_calendar\n- d (TEXT): Day key\n- date (DATE): Real calendar date\n\nRelationship:\n- m5_sales_train.d = m5_calendar.d\n\nBusiness meaning:\n- m5_sales_train is the forecasting fact table.\n- sales is the forecasting target.\n- m5_calendar provides the real calendar date.\n- Always use m5_calendar.date as the true time axis.\n\n\nSQL GENERATION RULES:\n\n- Use m5_sales_train as the fact table with alias s.\n- Always join m5_calendar as alias c on s.d = c.d.\n- Always return exactly two columns: ds and y.\n- For day granularity, use c.date as ds.\n- For month granularity, use DATE_TRUNC('month', c.date)::date AS ds.\n- For quarter granularity, use DATE_TRUNC('quarter', c.date)::date AS ds.\n- For year granularity, use DATE_TRUNC('year', c.date)::date AS ds.\n- Aggregate the forecasting target with SUM(s.sales) AS y.\n- Support filters on item_id, dept_id, cat_id, store_id and state_id.\n- A logical date filter must be translated to c.date after joining m5_calendar.\n- Group by the selected ds expression.\n- Sort by ds ascending.\n- Generate only one SELECT statement.\n\n\nAllowed granularities and horizons:\n- day: 7, 28, 30